ttribute("aria-expanded")==="true";shutAll();set(b,!was);return;} if(!inside){shutAll();} }); document.addEventListener("keydown",function(e){ if(e.key!=="Escape"&&e.keyCode!==27){return;} var n=triggers(),i; for(i=0;i<n.length;i++){ if(n[i].getAttribute("aria-expanded")==="true"){set(n[i],false);n[i].focus();} } }); })();'
  abstract: |
    Machines that improve themselves using their own outputs now exist and work, and there is no accepted science of what limits them. This paper proposes that science and stakes its claim the way thermodynamics was staked in 1824: not by declaring a field, but by computing a bound that any such machine must obey if the proposal is right, publishing the instruments that measure its terms, and preregistering by timestamp the experiments whose nulls favour the rival view. The field, Recursive Dynamics, takes the self-improvement loop as its native object; proposes five substrate-independent state variables written exactly as the programme's notation register defines them (capability, recursive depth, correction rate, drift, correction leverage); carries five laws as named conjectures with statuses declared, of which one, the ARC Ceiling, is derived in full from two lines of assumption, and two, added on 24 September 2026, have their mathematics set out at version 1.0 and are neither registered as laws nor tested; and locates its identity, as thermodynamics does, in its impossibilities: if the laws hold, self-improvement cannot outrun its own correction, the growth exponent is capped by the reciprocal of the correction shortfall, and no ladder of same-class oversight climbs past its ceiling by adding rungs, so the engineering lever is what the corrector is made of. Stated as prohibitions, so that no reader mistakes the paper's concessions for silence: the field forbids a stable system holding its growth exponent above the ceiling for a sustained run; a corrector-class contrast that runs the other way, or that falls wholly below the preregistered support threshold, which are the decisive trial's own anti-directional and equivalence verdicts; and monotone returns with no interior maximum as reinvestment rises. Any of these, observed under the preregistered analyses, makes the field wrong. Two things about that list are stated here rather than left for a reader to discover. A same-class corrector whose correction leverage measures wholly above one half is a prohibition of a different weight: it kills the one-half cap and the value two that follows from it, while the ceiling relation stands, because the relation returns whatever leverage exponent is measured. And a true null on the trial's six-family roster returns an inconclusive verdict at the preregistered precision rather than an equivalence verdict, an outcome that is reported as a failed attempt to confirm and never as a refutation. Before any of that, the paper does the thing a demarcation usually refuses: it tries to house its questions inside twelve neighbouring fields in their own variables, concedes what each already holds (the first law to endogenous growth theory, the form of the ceiling to queueing theory, the shape of the second law to error-threshold theory), prints where every part except the two laws added on 24 September 2026 would go if the field died, and isolates the one coupling no host can state. It then does the thing a founding proposal usually skips: it collects every objection to founding the field that its author and his adversarial readers could find, fifty-one of them, states each in its strongest form, and prints a disposition for each, conceding thirty-eight in full or in part, rejecting eleven with reasons, and handing two to experiment or to reading. The case for the field is scored against six licence conditions with the evidence for each; the precedent class of fields founded on a limit theorem in their own variables is named with its disanalogy; the founding conjunction, the set of results no neighbouring field could state in its own variables, is separated into what is preregistered today and what is only proposed; and the four results that would dissolve the field are printed with a commitment to publish them under this title. Its honest status is the Carnot stage: one memoir, instruments built, decisive measurements preregistered by timestamp and not run, staked where failure will be as visible as success.

